-- issue #1275: THE BYSTANDER, and the single variable of the whole fixture.
-- main.mdk neither imports this module nor names `MB` from it; it reaches the
-- loaded graph only via ifacea.mdk's bare `import bys`.
--
-- Renaming this interface `MZ` -- changing NOTHING else anywhere -- makes the
-- program REJECT correctly (`No impl of MB for Blob`, exit 1). Keeping the name
-- `MB` makes it print `1` at exit 0. That is the defect: `usePathWitnesses`
-- (compiler/types/typecheck.mdk) compares the candidate's interface NAME string,
-- so this declaration becomes a second "witnessed" candidate for main.mdk's
-- import, the `[only]` guard in `importedMethodEntry` declines, and the
-- pre-A-2.5 last-write-wins floor stands.
--
-- It must declare BOTH the same interface NAME and the same METHOD name -- that
-- is `usePathNamesMember` and `usePathBindsName` respectively.
export interface MB a where
  mth : a -> Int
